---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/RealestateLayout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="GTA Home Buyer's Guide | Cory Wong, Real Estate Agent | Trustwell Realty"
  description="A comprehensive guide to buying a home in the Greater Toronto Area. Pre-approval, TRESA, the offer process, due diligence, closing costs, and a step-by-step timeline."
  canonicalPath="/resources/buyer-guide"
>
  <!-- Page Hero -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="page-hero__title">The GTA Home Buyer's Guide</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__byline">By Cory Wong, Real Estate Agent</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Guide Content -->
  <article class="guide">
    <div class="container content-narrow">

      <!-- Table of Contents -->
      <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
        <h2 class="toc__title">In This Guide</h2>
        <ol class="toc__list">
          <li><a href="#pre-approval">Getting Pre-Approved</a></li>
          <li><a href="#buyer-representation">Buyer Representation in Ontario</a></li>
          <li><a href="#search-and-offer">Search and Offer Process</a></li>
          <li><a href="#due-diligence">Due Diligence</a></li>
          <li><a href="#closing-costs">Closing Costs</a></li>
          <li><a href="#timeline">Timeline: Offer to Close</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <!-- Section 1: Getting Pre-Approved -->
      <section id="pre-approval" class="guide__section">
        <h2 class="guide__section-title">1. Getting Pre-Approved</h2>
        <p>
          Before you start looking at homes, you need to know what you can afford. A
          mortgage pre-approval gives you a clear price range and shows sellers you're a
          serious buyer.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">What You'll Need</h3>
        <ul class="guide__list">
          <li>Proof of income (employment letter, pay stubs, or T4s; for self-employed buyers, two years of Notice of Assessments and financial statements)</li>
          <li>Credit report (your lender will pull this; a score above 680 gives you access to the best rates)</li>
          <li>Down payment verification (bank statements showing the source and accumulation of funds)</li>
          <li>Information on existing debts (car loans, student loans, credit card balances)</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">The Stress Test</h3>
        <p>
          All federally regulated lenders are required to qualify you at the higher of 5.25%
          or your contract rate plus 2%. This means if your actual mortgage rate is 4.5%, you
          must qualify at 6.5%. The stress test reduces your maximum borrowing power but exists
          to ensure you can handle rate increases over the life of your mortgage.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">First Home Savings Account (FHSA)</h3>
        <p>
          The FHSA lets first-time buyers save up to $8,000 per year (lifetime maximum of
          $40,000) in a registered account. Contributions are tax-deductible &mdash; like an
          RRSP &mdash; and withdrawals for a qualifying home purchase are completely tax-free,
          like a TFSA. If you're planning to buy within the next few years, opening an FHSA
          should be one of your first steps.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Down Payment Rules</h3>
        <ul class="guide__list">
          <li><strong>5% minimum</strong> on the first $500,000 of the purchase price</li>
          <li><strong>10%</strong> on the portion between $500,000 and $1,499,999</li>
          <li><strong>20% minimum</strong> on purchase prices of $1,500,000 or more</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If your down payment is less than 20%, you'll need CMHC mortgage default insurance.
          The premium (ranging from 2.8% to 4% of the mortgage amount) is added to your
          mortgage balance. While it's an additional cost, it allows you to enter the market
          with a smaller down payment and often comes with a slightly lower interest rate.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Buyer Representation -->
      <section id="buyer-representation" class="guide__section">
        <h2 class="guide__section-title">2. Buyer Representation in Ontario</h2>
        <p>
          Ontario's real estate regulations changed significantly when the Trust in Real
          Estate Services Act (TRESA) replaced the Real Estate and Business Brokers Act
          (REBBA) in 2023. Understanding these changes matters because they directly affect
          your rights and obligations as a buyer.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Buyer Representation Agreement (BRA)</h3>
        <p>
          Under TRESA, a signed Buyer Representation Agreement is now required before an
          agent can show you properties. This isn't just a formality &mdash; it establishes
          your agent's fiduciary duties to you, including loyalty, confidentiality, and the
          obligation to act in your best interests.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Fiduciary Duties</h3>
        <p>
          Once you sign a BRA, your agent owes you fiduciary duties. That means they must
          disclose all material facts they're aware of, negotiate on your behalf, keep your
          personal and financial information confidential, and provide honest advice &mdash;
          even if it means recommending you walk away from a property.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Commission Structure</h3>
        <p>
          Buyer agent compensation is typically outlined in the BRA. In many transactions,
          the seller offers compensation to the buyer's agent as part of the listing agreement.
          Your BRA will specify what happens if the seller's offered compensation differs from
          the agreed rate. It's important to understand this before you start your search, and
          your agent should explain it clearly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Search and Offer Process -->
      <section id="search-and-offer" class="guide__section">
        <h2 class="guide__section-title">3. Search and Offer Process</h2>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Defining Your Criteria</h3>
        <p>
          Start by separating needs from wants. Needs are non-negotiable: number of bedrooms,
          proximity to work or school, budget ceiling. Wants are preferences: a finished
          basement, a specific street, a south-facing backyard. Clarity on this distinction
          saves time and prevents decision paralysis when inventory is moving quickly.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">MLS and TRREB</h3>
        <p>
          The Toronto Regional Real Estate Board (TRREB) operates the MLS system that lists
          the vast majority of resale properties in the GTA. Your agent will set up automated
          searches based on your criteria so you're notified the moment a matching property
          hits the market.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Showings</h3>
        <p>
          Once you've identified properties of interest, your agent will arrange showings.
          During showings, look beyond cosmetics &mdash; pay attention to layout, natural
          light, storage, the condition of mechanical systems, and the neighbourhood itself.
          Drive by at different times of day if you're serious about a property.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Making an Offer</h3>
        <p>
          When you've found the right property, your agent will prepare an Agreement of
          Purchase and Sale. Key components include:
        </p>
        <ul class="guide__list">
          <li><strong>Price:</strong> Based on a Comparative Market Analysis (CMA) of recent comparable sales, active listings, and expired listings in the area</li>
          <li><strong>Conditions:</strong> Financing, home inspection, status certificate review (for condos), and any other protections you need</li>
          <li><strong>Deposit:</strong> Typically 5% of the purchase price, held in trust</li>
          <li><strong>Closing date:</strong> Usually 30 to 90 days from acceptance</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Competing Offers</h3>
        <p>
          In a competitive situation, the seller's agent may use a hold-back strategy &mdash;
          setting an offer date and reviewing all offers at once. In this scenario, you'll
          need to decide how aggressive to be on price and whether to waive or shorten
          conditions. Your agent's experience with competing offers is critical here: they
          should help you understand the risks and position your offer strategically without
          overextending.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Due Diligence -->
      <section id="due-diligence" class="guide__section">
        <h2 class="guide__section-title">4. Due Diligence</h2>
        <p>
          If your offer includes conditions, the conditional period (typically 5 to 10
          business days) is your window to verify that the property is what you expect
          and that your financing is confirmed.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Home Inspection</h3>
        <p>
          A qualified home inspector will examine the property's structure, roof, electrical,
          plumbing, HVAC, and other systems. Expect to pay $400 to $700 depending on the
          size and age of the home. Attend the inspection yourself &mdash; a good inspector
          will walk you through their findings and help you understand what's significant and
          what's normal wear.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Status Certificate (Condos)</h3>
        <p>
          If you're buying a condo, your lawyer will review the status certificate, which
          includes the condo corporation's financial statements, reserve fund study, rules
          and bylaws, and any pending litigation or special assessments. This document reveals
          the financial health of the building and any upcoming costs you should know about.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Financing Condition</h3>
        <p>
          Even with a pre-approval, your lender needs to approve the specific property. This
          includes an appraisal to confirm the property's value supports the mortgage amount.
          Occasionally, an appraisal comes in below the purchase price, which can require
          renegotiation or a larger down payment.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">FINTRAC Identity Verification</h3>
        <p>
          Under federal anti-money-laundering regulations, your agent is required to verify
          your identity through FINTRAC (Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre
          of Canada). This involves providing government-issued photo identification and
          confirming the source of your funds. It's a standard compliance requirement in
          every real estate transaction.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Closing Costs -->
      <section id="closing-costs" class="guide__section">
        <h2 class="guide__section-title">5. Closing Costs (1.5&ndash;4% of Purchase Price)</h2>
        <p>
          Closing costs are often underestimated by first-time buyers. Budget 1.5% to 4%
          of the purchase price beyond your down payment.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Land Transfer Tax</h3>
        <p>
          This is typically the largest closing cost. Ontario charges a provincial land
          transfer tax on all purchases, and the City of Toronto charges an additional
          municipal land transfer tax for properties within city limits.
        </p>
        <ul class="guide__list">
          <li><strong>Provincial LTT first-time buyer rebate:</strong> up to $4,000</li>
          <li><strong>Toronto municipal LTT first-time buyer rebate:</strong> up to $4,475</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Example:</strong> On a $900,000 purchase in Toronto, total land transfer
          tax is approximately $28,000 (before any first-time buyer rebates). The same
          purchase outside Toronto would be approximately $14,000 (provincial LTT only).
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Legal Fees</h3>
        <p>
          Your real estate lawyer handles title searches, document preparation, registration,
          and the transfer of funds. Expect to pay $1,500 to $2,500 including disbursements.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Title Insurance</h3>
        <p>
          Title insurance protects against defects in title, survey issues, and certain types
          of fraud. It's a one-time cost of $300 to $500 and is required by most lenders.
        </p>

        <h3 class="guide__subsection-title">Other Closing Costs</h3>
        <ul class="guide__list">
          <li>Property tax and utility adjustments (prorated from closing date)</li>
          <li>Home insurance (required before closing)</li>
          <li>Moving costs</li>
          <li>Immediate repairs or upgrades</li>
          <li>Condo reserve fund contribution (new builds)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6: Timeline -->
      <section id="timeline" class="guide__section">
        <h2 class="guide__section-title">6. Timeline: Offer to Close</h2>
        <p>
          A typical closing timeline runs 30 to 90 days. Here's what happens at each stage:
        </p>

        <div class="timeline">
          <div class="timeline__item">
            <div class="timeline__label">Day 1</div>
            <div class="timeline__content">
              <strong>Offer accepted.</strong> Your deposit (typically 5% of purchase price)
              is delivered to the listing brokerage within 24 hours and held in trust until closing.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline__item">
            <div class="timeline__label">Days 1&ndash;10</div>
            <div class="timeline__content">
              <strong>Conditional period.</strong> Home inspection, status certificate review
              (condos), financing confirmation, and any other conditions are fulfilled or the
              deal is renegotiated. Once all conditions are waived, the deal becomes firm and binding.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline__item">
            <div class="timeline__label">Days 10&ndash;50</div>
            <div class="timeline__content">
              <strong>Lawyer and lender preparation.</strong> Your lawyer conducts title
              searches, prepares transfer documents, and coordinates with your lender on
              mortgage instructions. Your lender finalizes the mortgage and sends instructions
              to your lawyer.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline__item">
            <div class="timeline__label">Days 50&ndash;60</div>
            <div class="timeline__content">
              <strong>Final walkthrough and funds.</strong> You'll do a pre-closing walkthrough
              to confirm the property's condition. Your lawyer will provide a statement of
              adjustments showing exactly what you owe. You arrange for the balance of funds
              to be available (certified cheque or wire transfer to your lawyer's trust account).
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline__item">
            <div class="timeline__label">Closing Day</div>
            <div class="timeline__content">
              <strong>Keys are yours.</strong> Your lawyer registers the transfer of title,
              your mortgage is registered, and funds are disbursed to the seller. You receive
              the keys &mdash; typically by mid-afternoon, though exact timing depends on
              registration processing.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <div class="guide__cta">
        <h2 class="guide__cta-title">Have Questions About Buying?</h2>
        <p class="guide__cta-text">
          Every purchase is different, and a guide can only cover so much. If you have
          questions about your specific situation &mdash; whether you're a first-time buyer
          or an experienced investor &mdash; book a consultation and get straightforward
          answers.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact" class="cta cta--primary">Book a Consultation</a>
      </div>

      <!-- Compliance -->
      <div class="guide__compliance">
        <p>
          Cory Wong, Real Estate Agent. Real estate services provided through Trustwell
          Realty Inc., Brokerage. This guide is intended for general informational purposes
          only and does not constitute legal, financial, or professional advice. Information
          is believed to be accurate as of early 2026 but is subject to change. Consult
          with qualified professionals for advice specific to your situation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- Newsletter -->
  <section class="newsletter">
    <div class="container content-narrow">
      <h2 class="newsletter__heading">Stay Informed</h2>
      <p class="newsletter__text">
        Get monthly market data, neighbourhood insights, and practical advice for buyers
        and sellers across the Greater Toronto Area.
      </p>
      <form id="newsletter-form" class="newsletter__form" novalidate>
        <input
          type="email"
          id="newsletter-email"
          name="email"
          placeholder="you@example.com"
          required
          autocomplete="email"
          class="newsletter__input"
        />
        <button type="submit" class="cta cta--primary newsletter__btn">Subscribe</button>
      </form>
      <p id="newsletter-form-status" class="form-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script>
  const newsletterForm = document.getElementById('newsletter-form') as HTMLFormElement | null;
  const newsletterStatus = document.getElementById('newsletter-form-status');

  if (newsletterForm && newsletterStatus) {
    newsletterForm.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      newsletterStatus.textContent = '';
      newsletterStatus.className = 'form-status';

      const formData = new FormData(newsletterForm);
      const payload = {
        type: 'newsletter',
        email: formData.get('email'),
      };

      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/lead', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        });

        if (res.ok) {
          newsletterStatus.textContent = 'You\'re subscribed! Watch your inbox for the next report.';
          newsletterStatus.classList.add('form-status--success');
          newsletterForm.reset();
        } else {
          throw new Error('Request failed');
        }
      } catch {
        newsletterStatus.textContent = 'Something went wrong. Please try again.';
        newsletterStatus.classList.add('form-status--error');
      }
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .content-narrow {
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  /* Page Hero */
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--space-2xl) 0 var(--space-xl);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .page-hero__title {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .page-hero__byline {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  /* Table of Contents */
  .toc {
    background: #f5f5f4;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .toc__title {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .toc__list {
    list-style: decimal;
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .toc__list li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .toc__list li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .toc__list a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .toc__list a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* Guide */
  .guide {
    padding: 0 0 var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .guide__section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .guide__section:last-of-type {
    border-bottom: none;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .guide__section-title {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .guide__subsection-title {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .guide__section p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .guide__section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .guide__list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }

  .guide__list li {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
    position: relative;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .guide__list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.625rem;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .guide__list li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Timeline */
  .timeline {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .timeline__item {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    padding: var(--space-md) 0;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
    margin-left: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    position: relative;
  }

  .timeline__item::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -7px;
    top: var(--space-md);
    width: 11px;
    height: 11px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .timeline__label {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    white-space: nowrap;
    min-width: 5.5rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-top: 0.125rem;
  }

  .timeline__content {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .timeline__content strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* CTA */
  .guide__cta {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding: var(--space-xl);
    background: #f5f5f4;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .guide__cta-title {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .guide__cta-text {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    max-width: 30rem;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .cta {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background-color 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .cta--primary {
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .cta--primary:hover {
    background: var(--color-accent-hover);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  /* Compliance */
  .guide__compliance {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .guide__compliance p {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Newsletter */
  .newsletter {
    padding: var(--space-2xl) 0;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: #ffffff;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .newsletter__heading {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .newsletter__text {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    opacity: 0.9;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .newsletter__form {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: 28rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .newsletter__input {
    flex: 1;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    padding: 0.625rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.3);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .newsletter__input::placeholder {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
  }

  .newsletter__input:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: #ffffff;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25);
  }

  .newsletter__btn {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border: 1px solid #ffffff;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .newsletter__btn:hover {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .form-status {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    min-height: 1.25rem;
  }

  .newsletter .form-status--success {
    color: #ffffff;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .newsletter .form-status--error {
    color: #fecaca;
  }

  /* Responsive */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .timeline__item {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-xs);
    }

    .timeline__label {
      min-width: auto;
    }

    .newsletter__form {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
